  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 220°C/200°C fan-forced.\n• Thinly slice brown onion. Finely chop or crush garlic.\n• Cut tomato into thin wedges. Cut zucchini into rounds. Cut lemon into wedges.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68b0eb7f45a3b6207f7e46ff/step-f8914000.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. Cook onion until softened, 3-4 mins.\n• Stir in tomato & herb seasoning, the stock powder, water and risotto rice. Bring to the boil, then remove from heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68b0eb7f45a3b6207f7e46ff/step-8954d010.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Transfer risotto to a large baking dish.\n• Cover tightly with foil and bake until liquid is absorbed and rice is ‘al dente’, 24-28 mins.\n• When risotto has 8 mins remaining, wipe out frying pan, then return to medium\u0002high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook tomato and zucchini, tossing, until softened, 4-5 mins.\n• Add garlic and cook until fragrant, 1 min.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68b0eb7f45a3b6207f7e46ff/step-1cc0e320.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Stir Parmesan cheese, the butter, a squeeze of lemon juice and baby spinach through risotto until spinach has wilted. Add a splash of water to loosen if needed.\n• Gently stir through cooked veggies. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\n• Divide risotto between bowls. Sprinkle with the chilli flakes (if using) and flaked almonds.\n• Serve with remaining lemon wedges.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/68b0eb7f45a3b6207f7e46ff/step-81c05030.jpeg"
    }
  ]
